/tailscale2otel
/bin/
/dist/
*.out
# Third-party notices are a RELEASE ARTIFACT (regenerated on every dependency bump by
# scripts/notices.sh, baked into the image, attached to the GitHub Release) — never committed.
/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local secrets, credentials, local config and captured data — NEVER commit.
#
# deploy/.env is the CANONICAL Compose credential file. `docker compose` reads
# its env file from the PROJECT directory — the directory holding the compose
# file — not from the shell's cwd, so `docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yaml`
# loads deploy/.env whichever directory you run it from. The root .env is covered
# too, for `docker run --env-file .env` and stray tooling.
#
# These patterns are deliberately UNANCHORED so they also match one level down
# (deploy/.env, deploy/.secrets/, deploy/.capture/, deploy/checkpoints/).
#
# WARNING: .gitignore is NOT a Docker build-context boundary — Docker never reads
# it. .dockerignore is the only thing keeping these files out of a build context,
# its layers and its cache. Add every new sensitive path to BOTH files.
# Both halves are gated by scripts/check-secret-hygiene.sh.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.env
.secrets/
config.local.yaml
config.smoke.yaml
config.lowlog.yaml
# Operator-supplied Docker secret files mounted by docker-compose.secrets.yaml (#334).
deploy/secrets/
# The operator-supplied file that docker-compose.config.yaml mounts (#333).
# Credentials belong in deploy/.env, but this is a real config file in a real
# tree and must not be committable by accident.
deploy/config.yaml
.smoke.yaml
# Checkpoint state (poller high-water marks). checkpoints.json is the default
# file store; deploy/docker-compose.yaml documents a ./checkpoints bind-mount
# beside itself, which lands at deploy/checkpoints/.
checkpoints.json
checkpoints/
# Captured real-tailnet data used only for local fixture authoring.
.capture/
# Non-secret templates stay committable. These negations MUST stay below the
# patterns above (last match wins), and note that a `!` re-include can never
# resurrect a file inside an excluded DIRECTORY — so never put a committed
# template inside .secrets/, .capture/ or checkpoints/.
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template

.DS_Store

# Local working copies of the Tailscale OpenAPI spec (root only). The committed,
# tracked baseline the drift CI diffs against is spec/tailscale-api.json — the
# leading slash here keeps these patterns from also ignoring that vendored copy.
/tailscale-api.json
/tailscale-api.yaml

docs/superpowers/
# Local long-running campaign goals and launch notes. Backlog tasks remain the
# durable run record; these coordination artifacts are never committed.
codex/
# Some tooling writes plans/specs to the repo root instead of docs/. Same rule
# applies wherever they land: brainstorming specs and implementation plans are
# scratch, never committed.
/superpowers/

2026-06-07-feature-roadmap.md

# Zensical docs-site build output
site/

# Codex security-scan findings (local review artifacts)
tailscale2otel-security-findings/

# Local scratch TODO/backlog notes — never committed (the old committed todos.txt
# was removed in the docs consolidation; keep any future scratch list local). #122
todos.txt

# Python bytecode cache — created by running the dashboard/alert generators
# (deploy/grafana/gen/build.py, deploy/alerts/gen/build_rules.py).
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# TEST-ONLY Prometheus rendering of the alert catalogue, written by
# `deploy/alerts/gen/build_rules.py --prom-out`. tailscale2otel ships
# Grafana-managed manifests only (deploy/alerts/grafana-managed/); this file
# exists purely so `promtool test rules` can EXECUTE the expressions, since
# promtool understands no other format. It must never be committed or shipped.
deploy/alerts/.generated-prom-rules.yaml

# Superpowers visual-companion scratch (brainstorming mockups)
.superpowers/

# Tool-module binaries left behind by a bare `go build` inside tools/<name>/.
# Go names the output after the directory, so it lands next to the source.
tools/*/promqlcheck
tools/*/metricscatalog
tools/*/configcheck
tools/*/apidrift

# Persistent flow-store databases (flows.store.directory), if one is ever pointed
# at the checkout. SQLite runs in WAL mode, so the sidecar files come too.
flows-*.db
flows-*.db-wal
flows-*.db-shm

# Injected by the m7kni.io hub at build time — never commit these.
# The hub copies its own SEO template, brand stylesheet and fonts into a clone
# and generates zensical.toml from docs.toml. A tracked copy here is drift, and
# is exactly what the manifest model exists to prevent.
/zensical.toml
docs/overrides/
docs/stylesheets/brand.css
docs/assets/project-icon.svg
docs/assets/project-icon-solid.svg
docs/assets/social-card.png
docs/assets/social-card.svg
docs/fonts/

# Claude Code repo-local config. `settings.json` and `hooks/` ARE tracked — they
.claude/

# Product-development candidate list — local working doc, evaluated into Backlog items manually
/candidates.md
